content.thinking:
The `hashchange` event fires asynchronously. The console.log "hash changed to: #/completed" appears after the main code finishes. So the `hashchange` event is fired, but not synchronously.

This means when the step definition sets the hash and then the next step tries to find the todo, the hashchange handler hasn't fired yet, so the filter hasn't been applied.

I need to fix the step definition to ensure the filter is applied after setting the hash. One approach is to manually call `render()` after setting the hash, or to dispatch the hashchange event synchronously.

Actually, looking at the app code, the filter link click handler does:```javascript


link.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
  e.preventDefault();
  window.location.hash = link.getAttribute('href').replace('#', '');
  render();
});```

